Shrine-Gain
Ingredients: AFROBEAT + ELECTROPOP + 432Hz RELAXING MEDITATIVE STYLES + NEURAL DSP ARCHETYPE GOJIRA X + 1960s ERA  
Creative Catalyst: Reverse-engineered from a corroded, half-demagnetized cassette unearthed from a 1968 municipal time capsule.

Shrine-Gain sounds like a high-energy Fela Kuti horn-and-percussion ensemble colliding with sparkling synth-pop hooks, submerged in warm 432Hz healing-tone drones, and suddenly cleaved open by down-tuned, pitch-shifted high-gain guitar slams dripping in vintage 1960s spring reverb.

Genre DNA
* Tempo & Pulse: 108–118 BPM. The bottom end trades between an insistent, danceable electro-pop four-on-the-floor kick and polyrhythmic Afrobeat syncopation, driven by organic shekere cross-rhythms and talk-drum accents.
* Harmonic Palette: Anchored strictly to A=432Hz tuning. Modal Dorian and Mixolydian highlife vamps built around clean brass and bright analog synth arpeggios, offset by crushing, pitch-shifted minor-second drop-tuned sludge stabs.
* Production Signatures: 
  1. Sub-Octave Pick-Scrape Gating: High-gain chugs dialed through the Archetype Gojira X neural model, pitch-shifted two octaves down, and sidechain-ducked beneath the dry strike of the shekere.
  2. Corrupted Tape Flutter: Warbling 1960s tape-head saturation applied directly to glossy synth leads and vocoded harmonies to emulate magnetic oxide decay.
  3. Meditative Drone Sub-Bed: A constant sinusoidal sub-bass bed and brass singing-bowl drone tuned to 432Hz, running beneath the rhythm section to induce physical bodily calm amidst chaos.
* Dynamics: Extended, hypnotic rhythmic trances build incrementally for several minutes through interlocking polyrhythms, exploding into four-bar walls of monolithic, fuzz-drenched heavy metal chugs before snapping cleanly back to serene, sparkling pop minimalism.

